      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "A room-temperature perovskite material yielding a power conversion efficiency of 18.1% (stabilized at 17.7%) is demonstrated by judicious selection of cations. Both cesium and methylammonium are necessary for room-temperature formamidinium-based perovskite to obtain the photoactive crystalline perovskite phase and high-quality crystals. This room-temperature-made perovskite material shows great potential for low-cost, large-scale manufacturing such as roll-to-roll processing."
      },
